  "body": "## What changed\n\n#2182 (#2177) makes the program sim judge a box stock that is turned a quarter about Z. This change is correct and on purpose (`docs/decisions/2177-square-stock-sim.md`). #2182 changed four suites that used the quarter turn as the device \"the sim does not judge\". Six other suites kept that device. Their checks that the operation's own clause holds the post saw the sim's gouge clause first. Thus 18 tests in `camcraft-app` went red on main (post-merge run 43977363817).\n\nThis PR changes only tests:\n\n- `circular_pick_law`, `trochoid_law`, `keep_law`, `kept_parts_live`, `stock_source_holes`, `pocket3d_open_side` turn the stock 1e-6 rad about Z (`OBLIQUE`), the device of #2177.\n- `pocket_support` gets `stock_turn`, `OBLIQUE` and `oblique_refused`, the twins of the `area_support` helpers.\n- Each check that the operation's own clause holds the post now also asserts that the sim refuses the stock by name (`stock_follow::OBLIQUE_STOCK`).\n- The fixture box checks take 1e-4 mm in X and Y. Z stays at 1e-9.\n\nNo \"never posts\" assert is removed. No refusal, gouge check or collision check changes.\n\n## Readings\n\nOn `7e26134bf` without this change:\n\n- 17 tests: the post is still refused. The sim clause leads, for example `post blocked - gouge: program cuts below the model in 4695 cell(s), worst 3.00 mm`.\n- 1 test (`stock_source_chamfer_refusal_names_cause_and_part_as_source_workaround`, case \"chamfer-rejudge-hint\"): the program POSTED. A stock-source 2D Chamfer cuts into a part that was added after generation. The same case also posts with an aligned stock, since #1628. The cause is in `posting_sim::judge_clause`: the live re-judge runs only when the sim does not judge. This PR does not fix that defect. It is #2308 (P1). With the oblique device, this suite again pins the re-judge where the sim does not judge.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nAll tests of the six suites pass with this change:\n\n- `circular_pick_law`: 5 passed\n- `trochoid_law`: 7 passed\n- `keep_law`: 31 passed\n- `kept_parts_live`: 4 passed\n- `stock_source_holes`: 9 passed\n- `pocket3d_open_side`: 7 passed\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The other suites that include `pocket_support` were compiled by clippy but not run. Their code is unchanged; the new helpers are additions.\n- No batch gate, no UI suites, no release lanes.\n- `pocket3d_open_side.rs` was 423 lines before this PR and is 422 lines now. It stays over the 400-line law; a split is not in this fix.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/2306-red-refusal-suites.md`.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #2306\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
